    "q-105758": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105758",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=8 \\\\ -8{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=8$ and ${y}_{2}=50.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
